  "body": "Hanene Street, St Heliers – Award-Winning Architecture, Extraordinary Harbour Views\r\n\r\nDiscover the residence: https://www.3and5hanene.com\r\n\r\nWinner of the 2026 TIDA New Zealand Renovation of the Year Award, this exceptional residence by Michael Cooper Architects offers the rare opportunity to own a nationally recognised home on one of Auckland’s most prestigious clifftop streets.\r\n\r\nWith breathtaking 270° harbour views, a prized north-facing aspect and an expansive 1,613 m² freehold estate, this is a property where remarkable architecture meets an extraordinary setting.\r\n\r\nRecognised in the Trends International Design Awards, the home’s transformation brings together architectural vision, meticulous craftsmanship and uncompromising luxury. Commanding a coveted double block above the Waitemata Harbour, its sweeping outlook stretches from Rangitoto Island to the Harbour Bridge.\r\n\r\nAcross four exquisite levels, generous living spaces connect effortlessly with sun-soaked terraces, resort-style entertaining areas and peaceful private retreats. The harbour provides an ever-changing backdrop, creating a home as memorable for everyday living as it is for entertaining on a grand scale.\r\n\r\nFive beautifully appointed bedrooms and eight luxurious bathrooms provide exceptional accommodation. The master suite is a private sanctuary, complete with its own terrace, panoramic views and a spa-inspired ensuite.\r\n\r\nA rooftop bar and panoramic viewing decks set the scene for unforgettable evenings, while a cinema, wine and whisky cellar, and private office offer spaces to unwind, entertain and work in comfort.\r\n\r\nAn internal lift connects the top three levels. On the lower level, a self-contained guest suite provides privacy and flexibility for visitors, extended family or staff.\r\n\r\nOutdoors, manicured grounds feature a tranquil water feature, putting green and a private path leading directly to Tamaki Drive—an exceptional connection to Auckland’s waterfront.\r\n\r\nFor enthusiasts and collectors, six-car garaging includes a separate Tamaki Drive–level garage, ideal for a Sealegs or classic car.\r\n\r\nMoments from St Heliers Bay’s cafés, beaches and sought-after schools, this remarkable residence combines coastal convenience with privacy, scale and architectural distinction.\r\n\r\nAn extraordinary waterfront setting. A nationally recognised design. A rare opportunity to make both your own.\r\n\r\nPrivate viewings by appointment only.\r\n\r\nPlease contact Brendan Goodwin on 021 278 7770 or email brendan@uniq.nz.\r\n\r\nPLEASE NOTE: The technical information provided (including floor plan and section sizes, for example) has been sourced from third-party organisations such as Cotality, LINZ, and Auckland Council. It is provided as a broad guide for general information only. It is intended to provide a general understanding of the subject matter.",
